a port of the serialize and unserialize functions of php to python. This module
implements the python serialization interface (eg: provides `dumps`, `loads` and
similar functions).

Reference-aware archive ordering
================================

`reorder_archive(data, new_order, allowed_objects=None)` reads a PHP archive
without loading classes, reorders/prunes its top-level list, and rewrites
`R:` variable aliases and `r:` object handles with valid new indices.

    output, reference_report = reorder_archive(
        data, ['C', 'B', 'D'], allowed_objects=allowed_positions)
    restored = loads(output, decode_strings=True)

`output` is bytes and also exposes `reference_sources`, `reference_map`, and
`missing_permissions`. Each report record contains the output reference id,
source byte offset, source path, and target position. `loads` automatically
uses live alias/object-sharing containers when `R:` or `r:` is present;
ordinary arrays continue through the original loader.
